  "learnBullets": [
    "Units of weight: **gram (g)** and **kilogram (kg)**",
    "The conversion rule: **1 kg = 1000 g**",
    "Adding and subtracting weights",
    "Comparing and ordering weights"
  ],
  "learnItFirst": "```\n1 kilogram (kg)  =  1000 grams (g)\n```\n\n**Converting kilograms to grams:** multiply by 1000\n```\n2 kg = 2 × 1000 = 2000 g\n```\n\n**Converting grams to kilograms:** divide by 1000 (works evenly for multiples of 1000)\n```\n3000 g = 3000 ÷ 1000 = 3 kg\n```\n\n**Adding/subtracting weights** — keep the unit the same:\n```\n250 g + 300 g = 550 g\n1 kg 200 g  =  1200 g   (1 kg = 1000 g, so 1000 + 200 = 1200)\n```\n\n### 🧠 How to Solve — 3 Easy Steps\n1. **Check the units** — are both weights in g, or in kg? Make them match first.\n2. **Convert** using 1 kg = 1000 g if needed.\n3. **Add, subtract, or compare** the numbers normally.\n\n---",
